# BiciMAD 2022 Visualization Project — Cursor Rules

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: React 19 + Vite, D3.js v7, Deck.gl v9, MapLibre GL
- **Preprocessing**: Python 3.11+, pandas, numpy, python-louvain
- **Styling**: Vanilla CSS with glassmorphism design system (no Tailwind/CSS-in-JS)
- **Icons**: lucide-react
- **Deployment**: Local only / zip submission (no SSR, no backend)

## Data Schema Quick Reference
- **Trip CSVs** (`bicimad_2022/trips_22_MM_*.csv`): Semicolon-delimited, CRLF, two schemas (19 cols Jan-Jul w/ idTrip, 18 cols Feb-Dec w/o). Every data row followed by filler row. Geolocation is Python literal (`ast.literal_eval`), coords are [lon, lat].
- **Station JSON** (`bicimad_2022/2022MM.json`): Line-delimited JSON, one snapshot per line, 264 stations each. Lat/lon are strings. `id` joins to CSV `station_unlock`/`station_lock`.
- **August 18–22 trip gap**: Exclude from all aggregations. JSON snapshots are complete for these dates.

## Coding Conventions
- Components: PascalCase `.jsx` files in `src/components/`
- UI primitives: `src/components/ui/Glass*.jsx`
- Hooks: `use*.js` in `src/hooks/`
- Utilities: `src/utils/`
- Preprocessing scripts: `scripts/*.py`, each independently runnable
- Pre-processed data output: `public/data/*.json`
- Use column names never positional indices for CSV parsing
- All D3 visualizations must be responsive (ResizeObserver pattern)
- Canvas rendering for OD matrix (264×264 = ~70K cells)

## Design System
- Background: #F5F3EF (warm off-white)
- Glass cards: rgba(255,255,255,0.6), backdrop-filter: blur(20px), border-radius: 16px
- Typography: system sans-serif, uppercase tracking for labels
- Accent: muted navy #1B2A4A
- Buttons: pill-shaped, transparent/glass, uppercase text
- Spacing: generous (24-32px padding)
